      "description": "Watch Lecce vs Monza highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 13, 2026. In a match played with the typical intensity of Serie A , Lecce and Monza delivered a compelling contest defined by shifts in momentum and clinical finishing. Held on September 13, 2026, the game pushed both sides to their physical and tactical limits throughout the ninety minutes. A Fast-Paced Opening Half Lecce began with explosive energy, grabbing an early lead just 3 minutes into the match when Lassana Coulibaly headed home from an Ivan Ilic corner. The home side maintained their aggressive stance, and by the 11th minute, Tiago Gabriel doubled the lead with another header, again set up by Ivan Ilic . Monza showed character, clawing one back in the 20th minute through Ricardo Mangas , who tapped home after good work from Jay Robinson and Samuele Birindelli . However, the joy was short-lived as Lassana Coulibaly netted his second of the day just a minute later, re-establishing a two-goal cushion for Lecce in a frantic start to the game. Tactical Shifts and Late Drama As the second half progressed, the game evolved into a tactical stalemate with both managers utilizing substitutes to influence the flow. Although Monza controlled the majority of possession at 61%, they struggled to penetrate the disciplined Lecce defense. The atmosphere grew tense in the 89th minute when Exequiel Zeballos curled a sublime direct free kick into the net following a fumble by goalkeeper Wladimiro Falcone . Despite a desperate late push from the visitors in stoppage time, Lecce held firm, ensuring they secured all three points despite the opponent's persistent efforts to equalize."
